    "created_at": "2015-11-19T00:25:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-11-19T00:25:46Z",
    "body": "Yeah. Maybe letting each sub document have its own policy is a better idea. So setting the mode to \"manual\" would disable restoration of the document's viewport as well as restoration of any scrollable in-document areas like `<textarea>`, `<select size>1>` and `<div style=\"overflow: scroll\"></div>`.\n\nBut it would not affect restoration inside an `<iframe>`. But of course the document inside the `<iframe>` could set its own policy.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
